Capture: convert 8-bit DMA-BUF captures of PQ outputs to SDR and describe
per-format encodings

8-bit DMA-BUF copies of a PQ output were plain blits that delivered 8-bit PQ
code values. Decode PQ and map SDR white back to 1.0, as the SHM path does.
Offer XRGB8888 first for SHM on PQ outputs, since first-pick clients such as
grim cannot describe PQ. Label unconverted output DMA-BUF frames with the
source encoding. aqueous-capture-color-v1 version 2 adds get_session_info,
which announces the expected encoding of every offered format so clients can
label streams before the first frame.

